  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 250 AM MDT SUN SEP 20 2026\nThe warming trend tapers off behind the Tuesday low pressure\nsystem, but continues to rise by a few degrees late this week. \nThursday is projected to be the warmest day of the long term as \na trough axis and associated cold front approach, allowing \nvalley temperatures to reach the mid to upper 80s. Temperatures \ndrop sharply behind the frontal passage Friday and Saturday, \nfalling below seasonal normals. Precipitation chances amongst\nguidance is still lower overall, but we'll likely see this\nchange as they come into better agreement on the timing of the\nfront.",
